    "code_released": "https://github.com/lca0503/Llama_tw",
    "peer_reviewed": "preprint",
    "problems": "The paper's ToxiGen evaluation is a toxicity-classifier measure, not a harmful-request refusal or compliance test. The authors state that they used only a Traditional Chinese corpus and that reproducing all continual-pretraining methods was resource-intensive. No uncertainty estimates are reported for the ToxiGen scores.",
    "rows_left_out": "No results omitted for the claim's subject; other reported outcomes, including truthfulness, bias sentiment, language identification, repetition, and knowledge benchmarks, are not direct measures of the safety behaviour in the claim.",
    "untested": [
      {
        "version": "V1",
        "parts": "No harmful fine-tuning data and no harmful-request compliance measure."
      },
      {
        "version": "V2",
        "parts": "Benign continual pre-training is done, but no harmful-request compliance or refusal rate is measured; only ToxiGen toxicity is reported."
      },
      {
        "version": "V3",
        "parts": "No per-token KL between aligned and base models."
      },
      {
        "version": "V4",
        "parts": "No prefilling, suffix or decoding attacks."
      },
      {
        "version": "V5",
        "parts": "The layer and module freezing and adapter variants are not evaluated for which weights carry refusal behaviour."
      },
      {
        "version": "V6",
        "parts": "No analysis of why safety is shallow."
      },
      {
        "version": "V7",
        "parts": "No safety-deepening training."
      }
    ],
    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "The record's uncertainty_reported 'y' is only partly true: BOLD sentiment has standard deviations, but ToxiGen scores have none. TW toxicity is scored by translating outputs to English with Google Translate before the classifier, which adds noise. The finding is adjacent to V2 (benign training erodes safety), but the measure is toxic text generation, not compliance with harmful requests."
  },
